## Candidate Lemma Shape
For every primitive LRC14 covering packet after the q-witness and LRC<=13 induction split, either:
  1. the even-speed 2-adic descent supplies a signed-SPEC floor packet with |SPEC| < product;
  2. HYP-3422 interval relocation supplies an E_safe half-lift overlap;
  3. the even-good window remains but odd danger arcs emit a positional phase-cover debt;
  4. the first mixed quotient is discharged by owner-current/Menger sidecar, with even-cover labels named;
  5. HYP-3421 off-grid transparency routes the signed-SPEC/Rprime branch;
  6. additive/multiplicative energy concentration converts to a low-SPEC penalty or named odd debt;
  7. HYP-3423 blocks q-uniform topology/Galois data from closing a q-specific floor;
  8. the packet is off-path 7-adic/census data and must be demoted unless it feeds one of the above.

## Assumption Challenge
Considered vertices: runners, gaps, fixed circle sections, section boundaries, wall-crossing events, residues, cover arcs, Fourier modes/SPEC bins, parity sectors, additive-pair shells, multiplicative-energy atoms, owner currents, quotient states, and proof obligations.
Chosen vertices: proof obligations and duality-transfer gates.  The quotient preserves the LRC covering-floor predicate only when it feeds the SPEC floor, the 2-adic descent, odd phase debt, finite owner sidecars, or an explicit HYP-3423 legality/off-path filter.  It destroys raw row identity, terminal 7-adic numerology, and scalar shadows.
